  "body": "## What changed\n\n- A flat Circular with a helix entry turns the start of each later ring. The new start is a vertex of the ring's own polygon. At that vertex, the predicted helix orbit keeps 0.01 mm from the orbits that the earlier rings flew.\n- After each ring, the kernel reads the descents that the ring flew. It uses the crossing law itself (`verify::crossed_pairs`, 0.01 mm and 0.001 mm chords). If a descent crosses a descent of an earlier ring, the operation is refused by name: `helix entry: the descent at ... crosses the descent of an earlier ring ...`.\n- The first ring and each ring without a conflict keep vertex 0. Plunge entry, ramp entry and the vault mode do not change.\n- The new logic is in `crates/motion/src/machining2d/circular_helix.rs`.\n- The test module of `circular.rs` moved to `circular_tests.rs` (the `#[path]` pattern). `circular.rs` was 411 lines. It is now 374 lines.\n\n## Cause\n\nAll rings of a flat Circular run the same level ladder. Thus the helix of each ring shares each level's depth band with the helix of each other ring. The descent puts each helix next to the ring start, and all rings started at the +X vertex. With stepover 2 and helix radius 1, the helices touched. The crossing law reported each pair, and verification blocked the post.\n\n## Tests\n\nNew pins in `crates/motion/tests/circular_helix_rings.rs`:\n\n- `a_multi_ring_helix_circular_has_no_crossing`: the issue's job (R10, Ø6, stepover 2, helix 1) and four more sizes, climb and conventional, at two centers. No crossing pair. Red before the fix (`feed moves 2 and 83 cross ...`, 22 pairs).\n- `the_issue_job_verifies_without_crossings`: full `verify` on the issue's job. No warning except `RapidInStock`. Red before the fix (Crossing).\n- `a_helix_that_cannot_stand_apart_is_refused_by_name`: helix radius 3 on a Ø6 cutter in R10 is refused by name. Other sizes generate with no crossing, or are refused by name. Red before the fix (it generated with crossings).\n- `every_ring_still_reaches_the_floor`: each ring still cuts its full circle at the floor.\n\nUnit tests: `circular_helix::tests` (halving order, orbit test, the reading) and `a_phase_turns_the_ring_start_only`.\n\nMutations:\n\n- Stagger off (phase always 0): the three generation pins go red, because the reading refuses the job.\n- Refusal off: `a_helix_that_cannot_stand_apart_is_refused_by_name` goes red.\n- The upstream `circular.rs`: three pins go red.\n\nGate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` is green (133 steps, 0 failed). `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean.\n\n## Expected test change\n\n`crates/app/tests/circular_arcs.rs::the_issue_table_posts_arcs_and_verifies_the_same`: three rows now expect the named refusal. On upstream, Crossing warnings already held each of them:\n\n| Row | Crossing warnings before |\n|---|---|\n| `helix_radius: 0.5` | 30 |\n| `radius: 4.0` | 154 |\n| `radius: 6.0` | 350 |\n\nThe radius rows were also the table's gouge check. They are judged again on a plunge entry, and they must still gouge.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. No `.nc` or `.cl` file changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The heavy lanes (`cargo xtask gate heavy`) did not run. They must run before this PR is flagged ready.\n- The app-level job of #2898 with a helix entry. The motion pin uses the same numbers.\n- The two `RapidInStock` warnings on the ring links. They are on upstream too, at the same move indices. #2898 owns them (claimed, no PR yet).\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- No open PR changes `circular.rs`.\n- #2898 has a live claim on the ring links of the same function `circular()`. It has no PR or branch yet. The PR that merges second refreshes.\n\nDecision record: `docs/decisions/3109-circular-helix-stagger.md`.\n\nEffort: high\n\nChangelog: Circular - a helix entry with several rings no longer makes helices that touch and block the post; each later ring starts where its helix stays clear, or the operation is refused by name.\n\nFixes #3109\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
